# ── Personal data — never commit ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMAP credentials for the job-alert inbox. App password lives here.
radar/inbox.json

# ntfy topic — anyone who knows it can read your job alerts
radar/.ntfy_topic

# Live application tracker: hiring-manager names, contact details, candid notes
# on role fit, and which jobs you have and have not applied to.
applications.md

# Strategy guides. These contain a candid assessment of one person's career -
# years of experience, where the background is thin, how recruiters will read
# it. Fine as private notes, not something to publish about yourself.
ats_job_finder_guide
ats_job_finder_guide_v2.md

# ── Generated state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which postings the radar has already shown you. Machine-local, rebuilt with
# `python3 job_radar.py --seed`. Binary, so it produces useless diffs.
radar/seen.sqlite3
radar/*.sqlite3
radar/*.sqlite3-journal
radar/*.sqlite3-wal
radar/*.sqlite3-shm

# The five rules above are pinned to radar/ and to the .sqlite3
# extension, which is two ways to miss a database. On 2026-10-22 a
# script that guessed the wrong filename created radar/jobs.db, and
# `git add .` staged it - it was empty, but a real one would have been a
# job history of every posting and employer seen. SQLite is created
# wherever a script happens to run, so match on extension, everywhere,
# for every suffix SQLite writes. The only database this repo expects is
# radar/seen.sqlite3, and it is never committed.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Output of the last run. Rewritten on every cron tick — pure churn.
radar/digest.md

# `inbox.py --md` output. Not credentials, but it is a transcript of the job
# alerts sent to a private address — which titles you watch, in which city.
# Same class as digest.md, so same treatment.
inbox.md
radar/inbox.md

# Append-only run history. Grows by a full digest every 30 minutes.
radar/radar.log
radar/web.log
radar/*.log
radar/.applications.lock
# Atomic-write scratch files. Normally renamed away instantly, but a crashed or
# killed write can leave one behind.
.tracker-*.tmp
*/.tracker-*.tmp

# Daily snapshots. These contain a full copy of applications.md, so they carry
# the same hiring-manager details the tracker does. Currently also caught by the
# generic *.bak rule below, but that is incidental - name this explicitly so a
# change to backup.sh's naming can never leak them.
backups/

# Employer tables regenerated by canada_employers.py (large, volatile).
# Delete these two lines if you would rather track them.
canada_employers.md
canada_employers_vendors.md

# ── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt and braces. The rules above name every log and secret this repo actually
# produces today; these catch the one a future script adds. A log is the usual
# way a credential escapes a program that was careful with it everywhere else.
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
*credentials*.json

*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
employers.txt
companies.txt

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
venv/
.venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
